{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Decision (operator, 2026-08-30): Approach B approved\n\nInstall uv ourselves from Astral's version-pinned release URL + committed sha256, wrapped in\n**one repo-local composite action** reused by the ~25 setup-uv call-sites (removes the\nper-job `raw.githubusercontent.com/.../uv.ndjson` artifact-URL fetch entirely). Rationale:\nonly option that can satisfy the AC (a real CI log with `Successfully installed uv <pin>` AND\nzero `Fetching manifest data`). Option A (actions/cache) only reduces the fetch — cold/evicted\ncache still hits the manifest, so the failure mode stays reachable. Option C (upstream\nsetup-uv patch) can't be scheduled on our timeline.\n\nPrecedent: Astral's version-pinned standalone installer is the canonical reproducible install;\nsetup-uv ships a `checksum:` input (checksum-pinned direct install is sanctioned); repo-local\ncomposite actions are standard GHA practice; internal precedent = we already pin+checksum\n`acli` (docs/jira-sync-setup.md).\n\n**Coordination:** touches `.github/workflows/` = eb64 declared scope; sibling 56b7 (the uv\npin) is the same file domain. Implement in coordination with eb64. The composite action lives\nunder `.github/actions/`; call-sites swap `uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@...` → `uses:\n./.github/actions/<name>`, preserving `enable-cache` behavior via the action."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788108471077898482,"uuid":"1a85a639-e675-49be-9d1f-ee798362a504"}